WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.910
 Real estate really,
really matters.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.790
It's the biggest financial
and emotional decision

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.189
that the average
person will make.

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:10.710
Real estate's the largest
segment of the global economy,

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.035
and nobody loves it.

00:00:13.035 --> 00:00:15.960
For many people it's hard
to wrap their head around.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.660
By taking this class,
I'm going to demystify

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.460
the entire process for you.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.580
I founded a real estate
technology platform.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.210
Its sole mission is to make
real estate better for everyone.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.670
There are a lot
of misconceptions

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.320
about the real estate industry.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.460
It's an industry that
powers single parents,

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.960
people like my mom, who
from a very early age

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.110
made me a dreamer.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:41.820
I saw her as an entrepreneur,
and it instilled in me

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.630
this desire to
create, build, dream,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.090
and be an entrepreneur myself.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.220
There's no blueprint
for buying a home,

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.040
but I am going to give you
some general guidelines of how

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.410
to approach it so that
you can be successful.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.230
I'm going to give
you an insider tip.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:02.370
When you're in an open house,
treat it like a flea market.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.439
Try not to share
your enthusiasm.

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.540
You want them to see
how confident you are,

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.330
but not that you need this.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.270
When you're a seller,
I highly urge you--

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.080
if you want to maximize
the value of your home,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.640
make it move-in ready.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.060
Homes that are move-in ready
sell faster than homes that

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.420
don't.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.830
Being raised with a single
parent where my father passed

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.250
away when I was young;
I've been searching

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.040
for belonging my entire life.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:35.590
I'm Black and Jewish, so
I never felt like I really

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:38.830
belonged in any category.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.070
Part of the dream was I was
going to create a family,

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:44.170
and this family would
be great; but it all

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.150
comes down to that home.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:50.650
A home is the culmination
of that belonging.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:54.100
Home creates stability,
security, memories.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.380
It's your place in the world.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.240
At the end of this
class, I want you

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.770
to feel like you
could dream bigger,

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.570
that anything is possible.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:04.870
Opportunity is
everywhere around you.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:10.530
I'm Robert Reffkin, and
this is my MasterClass.

